Hi,

I have a Compaq EVO N1020v notebook, and I'm using Linux 2.6.7-ck1.
When entering the S3 state via echo 3 > /proc/acpi/sleep, my system
suspends fine, but I cannot find a way to resume it. The power led is
blinking, which is fine I guess, but pressing buttons on the keyboard
(also combinations with Fn), does not bring the system back alive, neither
does the power button.

The only way out, is to hold the power button for several seconds until
the machine is powered down completely (power led stops blinking).

What could be the cause for this problem?

Frederik



